.PP
Caveats that impact the benchmark (and accuracy of comparison):

.PP
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRMap\fPs, \fRPromise\fPs, and \fRSet\fPs were excluded from the benchmark entirely because no library other than \fRdeep-eql\fP fully supported their comparison
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRfast-deep-equal\fP, \fRreact-fast-compare\fP and \fRnano-equal\fP throw on objects with \fRnull\fP as prototype (\fRObject\&.create(null)\fP)
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRassert\&.deepStrictEqual\fP does not support \fRNaN\fP or \fRSameValueZero\fP equality for dates
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRdeep-eql\fP does not support \fRSameValueZero\fP equality for zero equality (positive and negative zero are not equal)
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRdeep-equal\fP does not support \fRNaN\fP and does not strictly compare object type, or date / regexp values, nor uses \fRSameValueZero\fP equality for dates
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRfast-deep-equal\fP does not support \fRNaN\fP or \fRSameValueZero\fP equality for dates
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRnano-equal\fP does not strictly compare object property structure, array length, or object type, nor \fRSameValueZero\fP equality for dates
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRreact-fast-compare\fP does not support \fRNaN\fP or \fRSameValueZero\fP equality for dates, and does not compare \fRfunction\fP equality
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRshallow-equal-fuzzy\fP does not strictly compare object type or regexp values, nor \fRSameValueZero\fP equality for dates
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRunderscore\&.isEqual\fP does not support \fRSameValueZero\fP equality for primitives or dates
.PP

.PP
All of these have the potential of inflating the respective library's numbers in comparison to \fRfast-equals\fP, but it was the closest apples-to-apples comparison I could create of a reasonable sample size\&. It should be noted that \fRreact\fP elements can be circular objects, however simple elements are not; I kept the \fRreact\fP comparison very basic to allow it to be included\&.
.SH "Development"
.PP
Standard practice, clone the repo and \fRnpm i\fP to get the dependencies\&. The following npm scripts are available:

.PP
.IP "\(bu" 2
benchmark => run benchmark tests against other equality libraries
.IP "\(bu" 2
build => build \fRmain\fP, \fRmodule\fP, and \fRbrowser\fP distributables with \fRrollup\fP
.IP "\(bu" 2
clean => run \fRrimraf\fP on the \fRdist\fP folder
.IP "\(bu" 2
dev => start webpack playground App
.IP "\(bu" 2
dist => run \fRbuild\fP
.IP "\(bu" 2
lint => run ESLint on all files in \fRsrc\fP folder (also runs on \fRdev\fP script)
.IP "\(bu" 2
lint:fix => run \fRlint\fP script, but with auto-fixer
.IP "\(bu" 2
prepublish:compile => run \fRlint\fP, \fRtest:coverage\fP, \fRtranspile:lib\fP, \fRtranspile:es\fP, and \fRdist\fP scripts
.IP "\(bu" 2
start => run \fRdev\fP
.IP "\(bu" 2
test => run AVA with NODE_ENV=test on all files in \fRtest\fP folder
.IP "\(bu" 2
test:coverage => run same script as \fRtest\fP with code coverage calculation via \fRnyc\fP
.IP "\(bu" 2
test:watch => run same script as \fRtest\fP but keep persistent watcher 
.PP

